# Trivy ignore list for the worker-image scan gate (`.worker-scan` in
# `.gitlab/ci/containers.yml`). Every entry must carry a rationale (in the
# comment block above it) and an expiry date in Trivy's own syntax:
# `CVE-....-.... exp:YYYY-MM-DD` (exactly one space, lowercase `exp:`).
# Trivy's plain ignore-file parser (`pkg/result/ignore.go`,
# `getExpirationDate`) only recognises the `exp:` prefix and drops an entry
# once that date passes (`Prune`), so expired entries stop being ignored and
# the scan gate fails again until the finding is re-reviewed. `expiring:` is
# NOT Trivy syntax: before WI#361 every entry here used it, the parser found
# no `exp:` field, and all six suppressions silently never expired. The
# `ci-config` validator (`validate_trivy_ignore` in
# `.gitlab/scripts/validate_config.py`) now rejects any non-comment line that
# does not match this syntax and any expiry more than six months out.
#
# Re-verified 2026-10-17 against the pinned 20261017T082437Z Debian snapshot
# and the Debian security tracker (WI#361 fix item 3):
# - The three perl CVEs previously suppressed here (CVE-2026-13221,
#   CVE-2026-42496, CVE-2026-8376) are FIXED at this snapshot
#   (bookworm-security perl 5.36.0-7+deb12u4, DLA-4821-1; trixie
#   5.40.1-6+deb13u1) and are no longer listed.
# - bookworm (kimi, pebble images) still ships vulnerable libsqlite3-0
#   3.40.1-2+deb12u2 and zlib1g 1:1.2.13.dfsg-1; trixie (opencode,
#   opencode2 images) ships the fixed 3.46.1-7+deb13u2 and
#   1:1.3.dfsg+really1.3.1-1.
# - openssh-client is still vulnerable in BOTH distros (bookworm
#   1:9.2p1-2+deb12u10, trixie 1:10.0p1-7+deb13u4).

# libpython3.11-stdlib -> libsqlite3-0: python3's sqlite3 stdlib module.
# opencode scripts/study_notes_config.py imports sqlite3 and is exercised by
# a build-time test gate. Still needed for the bookworm images (kimi,
# pebble); trixie ships the fixed 3.46.1-7+deb13u2, so this entry is inert
# for opencode/opencode2. Revisit when the next-gen study-notes config lands.
CVE-2025-7458 exp:2027-04-17

# openssh-client is required for git+ssh worker operation (CVE-2026-60002 is
# a client-side UAF during host key re-exchange). Still vulnerable in both
# bookworm and trixie at the 20261017T082437Z snapshot, so all four worker
# images need this entry.
CVE-2026-60002 exp:2027-04-17

# zlib1g CVE-2023-45853 affects the minizip code path Debian's zlib1g does
# not ship; wontfix upstream. git itself Depends: zlib1g. Still needed for
# the bookworm images (kimi, pebble: zlib 1:1.2.13.dfsg-1 vulnerable);
# trixie's zlib 1:1.3.dfsg+really1.3.1-1 is fixed, so this entry is inert
# for opencode/opencode2. (bookworm's separate minizip package is fixed at
# 1.1-8+deb12u1; the suppression covers zlib1g only.)
CVE-2023-45853 exp:2027-04-17
